    "text": "To determine the measure of the smallest interior angle of a triangle with angles in the ratio 5:6:7, we start by letting the measures of the angles be \\(5x\\), \\(6x\\), and \\(7x\\). The sum of the interior angles of a triangle is always \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\n\\[\n5x + 6x + 7x = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n18x = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTo find the value of \\(x\\), we divide both sides of the equation by 18:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{180^\\circ}{18} = 10^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find the measures of the three angles by substituting \\(x = 10^\\circ\\) back into the expressions for the angles:\n\n\\[\n5x = 5 \\times 10^\\circ = 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n6x = 6 \\times 10^\\circ = 60^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n7x = 7 \\times 10^\\circ = 70^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThe smallest interior angle is \\(50^\\circ\\). Therefore, the measure of the smallest interior angle is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{50}\n\\]",
